<div id="p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent ltx_align_center"><span class="ltx_rule" style="width:397.5pt;height:4.0pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span>
<p id="p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Appendix</span>
<span class="ltx_rule" style="width:397.5pt;height:1.2pt;--ltx-bg-color:black;display:inline-block;"> </span></p>
</div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Use of Large Language Models</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the preparation of this manuscript, we employed a large language model (ChatGPT, developed by OpenAI) as a writing assistant. The model was used exclusively to:</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Improve the clarity, coherence, and conciseness of the text.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Rephrase sentences to enhance grammatical correctness and readability.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Ensure consistent terminology and smooth transitions across sections.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">All outputs generated by the LLM were carefully reviewed, edited, and validated by the authors to guarantee technical accuracy, logical consistency, and fidelity to the research content. No text was included without human oversight. Importantly, the LLM was not employed for data generation, model training, or experimental design.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Lemmas used in Proofs</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The first lemma provides a convergence rate for approximating the delta function using exponential sums.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,m\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,m\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{m}^{\exp}(t)=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{m}\alpha_{k}e^{-\beta_{k}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>exp</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{m}^{\exp}(t)=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{m}\alpha_{k}e^{-\beta_{k}t}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx4" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\mathbb{I}(\cdot=T)-\phi_{m}^{\rm exp}(\cdot)}\|_{\ell_{1}(\mathbb{N})}\leq\frac{1.3\ e^{0.02T}}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>exp</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\mathbb{I}(\cdot=T)-\phi_{m}^{\rm exp}(\cdot)}\|_{\ell_{1}(\mathbb{N})}\leq\frac{1.3\ e^{0.02T}}{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> holds for any <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A2.Thmlemma1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A,C&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A,C&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> are absolute constants.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">This lemma is a corollary of Lemma F.1 in  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang &amp; E (2024)</a></cite>. By Lemma F.1 in  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib66" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang &amp; E (2024)</a></cite> and its proof: for any <math id="A2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q,m\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q,m\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a <math id="A2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(q)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(q)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and a <math id="A2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{m}^{\exp}(t)=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{m}\alpha_{k}e^{-\beta_{k}t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>exp</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{m}^{\exp}(t)=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{m}\alpha_{k}e^{-\beta_{k}t}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx5" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\mathbb{I}(\cdot=T)-\phi_{m}^{\rm exp}(\cdot)}\|_{\ell_{1}(\mathbb{N})}\leq\frac{C(q)e^{0.01(q+1)T}}{m^{q}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>exp</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>0.01</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><msup><mi>m</mi><mi>q</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\mathbb{I}(\cdot=T)-\phi_{m}^{\rm exp}(\cdot)}\|_{\ell_{1}(\mathbb{N})}\leq\frac{C(q)e^{0.01(q+1)T}}{m^{q}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{k}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{k}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> holds for any <math id="A2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k\in[m]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k\in[m]</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx6" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle C(q)=\frac{M(q)}{(1-1/e)^{q}},\quad M(q)=\max_{0\leq k\leq q}\sup_{x\in[-1,1]}\left|\Psi^{(k)}(x)\right|," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>e</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>q</mi></msup></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>max</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></munder><mprescripts></mprescripts><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mrow></mrow></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em">⁡</mo><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle C(q)=\frac{M(q)}{(1-1/e)^{q}},\quad M(q)=\max_{0\leq k\leq q}\sup_{x\in[-1,1]}\left|\Psi^{(k)}(x)\right|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.3.1" class="ltx_text">where <math id="A2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Psi(x)=\begin{cases}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{1-x^{2}}\right),\ x\in(-1,1)\\
0,\ \mathrm{otherwise}\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Ψ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mi>otherwise</mi></mrow></mtd><mtd></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Psi(x)=\begin{cases}\exp\left(-\frac{1}{1-x^{2}}\right),\ x\in(-1,1)\\
0,\ \mathrm{otherwise}\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math> is the standard bump function on <math id="A2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[-1,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[-1,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. We mainly focus on small <math id="A2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>q</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q</annotation></semantics></math> since <math id="A2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(q)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(q)</annotation></semantics></math> grows rapidly and through directly computation, we have <math id="A2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C(1)\approx 1.3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>1.3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C(1)\approx 1.3</annotation></semantics></math> . Hence,</span></p>
<table id="A2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\|{\mathbb{I}(\cdot=T)-\phi_{m}^{\rm exp}(\cdot)}\|_{\ell_{1}(\mathbb{N})}\leq\frac{1.3\ e^{0.02T}}{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>exp</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≤</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mi>m</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{\mathbb{I}(\cdot=T)-\phi_{m}^{\rm exp}(\cdot)}\|_{\ell_{1}(\mathbb{N})}\leq\frac{1.3\ e^{0.02T}}{m}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.4.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma guarantees that, with high probability, a bounded random vector can be projected onto a <math id="A2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional subspace such that the resulting error, after applying any linear transformation <math id="A2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math>, is tightly controlled by <math id="A2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|A\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>A</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|A\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the projection dimension, and the vector’s norm bound.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(High-probability projection)<span id="A2.Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}</annotation></semantics></math> be a random vector with zero mean, identity covariance <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[\bm{x}\bm{x}^{\top}]=I_{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mi>D</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[\bm{x}\bm{x}^{\top}]=I_{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, and almost surely bounded norm <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{x}\|_{2}\leq B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{x}\|_{2}\leq B</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐀</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{A}\in\mathbb{R}^{m\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> be any fixed matrix. Then, for any <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an orthogonal projection matrix <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐏</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> such that with probability at least <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math> over the randomness of <math id="A2.Thmlemma2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐏</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex19" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{A}\bm{x}-\bm{A}\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P}\bm{x}\|_{2}\leq\|\bm{A}\|_{2}\,B\,\sqrt{1-\frac{d}{D}}\;\left(1+\sqrt{\frac{2\log(2/\delta)}{d}}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0.280em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{A}\bm{x}-\bm{A}\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P}\bm{x}\|_{2}\leq\|\bm{A}\|_{2}\,B\,\sqrt{1-\frac{d}{D}}\;\left(1+\sqrt{\frac{2\log(2/\delta)}{d}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">We construct <math id="A2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> as a random orthogonal projection (e.g., by taking the first <math id="A2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math> rows of a Haar-distributed orthogonal matrix, or using a Johnson-Lindenstrauss style random matrix). Then</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{A}\bm{x}-\bm{A}\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P}\bm{x}\|_{2}=\|\bm{A}(I-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}\leq\|\bm{A}\|_{2}\,\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑨</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>I</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{A}\bm{x}-\bm{A}\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P}\bm{x}\|_{2}=\|\bm{A}(I-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}\leq\|\bm{A}\|_{2}\,\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">From properties of random orthogonal projections, the squared projection error satisfies</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}^{2}=\|\bm{x}\|_{2}^{2}\left(1-\frac{d}{D}\right)\leq B^{2}\left(1-\frac{d}{D}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mi>d</mi><mi>D</mi></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}^{2}=\|\bm{x}\|_{2}^{2}\left(1-\frac{d}{D}\right)\leq B^{2}\left(1-\frac{d}{D}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Moreover, the projection error <math id="A2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> is a sub-Gaussian random variable with mean at most <math id="A2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\sqrt{1-d/D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\sqrt{1-d/D}</annotation></semantics></math>, so by a standard sub-Gaussian tail bound (Hoeffding inequality):</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\Big[\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}\geq B\sqrt{1-d/D}\,(1+t)\Big]\leq 2\exp\Big(-\frac{dt^{2}}{2}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≥</mo><mi>B</mi><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\Big[\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}\geq B\sqrt{1-d/D}\,(1+t)\Big]\leq 2\exp\Big(-\frac{dt^{2}}{2}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Taking <math id="A2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=\sqrt{\frac{2\log(2/\delta)}{d}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=\sqrt{\frac{2\log(2/\delta)}{d}}</annotation></semantics></math> gives</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}\leq B\sqrt{1-d/D}\left(1+\sqrt{\frac{2\log(2/\delta)}{d}}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑷</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}^{\top}\bm{P})\bm{x}\|_{2}\leq B\sqrt{1-d/D}\left(1+\sqrt{\frac{2\log(2/\delta)}{d}}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">with probability at least <math id="A2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>. Multiplying by <math id="A2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{A}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑨</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{A}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> completes the proof.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p8.1" class="ltx_p">The following lemma is Corollary 1 in  <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib49" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mudarisov et al. (2025)</a></cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.3</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{Logits}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Logits</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{Logits}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded, the attention weights satisfy:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{L}\exp\left(-2\Delta\right)\leq\|\mathrm{AttnScore}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{1}{L}\exp\left(2\Delta\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>AttnScore</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{L}\exp\left(-2\Delta\right)\leq\|\mathrm{AttnScore}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})\|_{\infty}\leq\frac{1}{L}\exp\left(2\Delta\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta=\|\bm{W}_{Q}\|_{2}\|\bm{W}_{K}\|_{2}B^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>B</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta=\|\bm{W}_{Q}\|_{2}\|\bm{W}_{K}\|_{2}B^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p9.1" class="ltx_p">The Gershgorin circle theorem localizes all eigenvalues of a matrix within discs determined by its diagonal entries and row sums of off-diagonal magnitudes.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.4</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Gershgorin circle theorem)<span id="A2.Thmlemma4.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A=(a_{ij})\in\mathbb{C}^{n\times n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℂ</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A=(a_{ij})\in\mathbb{C}^{n\times n}</annotation></semantics></math>. For each <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> define the Gershgorin radius</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R_{i}:=\sum_{j\neq i}|a_{ij}|." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R_{i}:=\sum_{j\neq i}|a_{ij}|.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Then every eigenvalue <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> lies in the union of the Gershgorin discs</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda\in\bigcup_{i=1}^{n}\{z\in\mathbb{C}:\ |z-a_{ii}|\leq R_{i}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">⋃</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda\in\bigcup_{i=1}^{n}\{z\in\mathbb{C}:\ |z-a_{ii}|\leq R_{i}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, if the discs <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{z:|z-a_{ii}|\leq R_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>z</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>R</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{z:|z-a_{ii}|\leq R_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math> are contained in a region <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S\subset\mathbb{C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mi>ℂ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S\subset\mathbb{C}</annotation></semantics></math>, then all eigenvalues of <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>A</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A</annotation></semantics></math> lie in <math id="A2.Thmlemma4.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>S</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">The mean value theorem expresses the difference
<math id="A2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F(\bm{y})-F(\bm{x})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F(\bm{y})-F(\bm{x})</annotation></semantics></math> as the Jacobian at an intermediate point applied to
<math id="A2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}-\bm{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}-\bm{x}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.5</span></span><span id="A2.Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Mean Value Inequality for vector-valued functions)<span id="A2.Thmlemma5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>m</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F:\mathbb{R}^{n}\to\mathbb{R}^{m}</annotation></semantics></math> be continuously differentiable on an open convex set <math id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D\subset\mathbb{R}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D\subset\mathbb{R}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then for any <math id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x},\bm{y}\in D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐲</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x},\bm{y}\in D</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists <math id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in(0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in(0,1)</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|F(\bm{y})-F(\bm{x})\|\leq\|JF(\bm{x}+\theta(\bm{y}-\bm{x}))\|\cdot\|\bm{y}-\bm{x}\|," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒚</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>F</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>𝒚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|F(\bm{y})-F(\bm{x})\|\leq\|JF(\bm{x}+\theta(\bm{y}-\bm{x}))\|\cdot\|\bm{y}-\bm{x}\|,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="JF(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>F</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">JF(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Jacobian matrix of <math id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="F" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>F</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">F</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmlemma5.p1.m7" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\cdot\|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\cdot\|</annotation></semantics></math> is an appropriate vector/matrix norm.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ Linear sequence modeling. ‣ 4 Parameter trade-offs in Information Extraction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we give the detailed proof of Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ Linear sequence modeling. ‣ 4 Parameter trade-offs in Information Extraction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. We first restate the theorem:</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem C.1</span></span><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restate of Theorem <a href="#S4" title="4 Parameter trade-offs in Information Extraction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>.)<span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To approximate the linear target <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\bm{\rho}_{i}\bm{x}_{t-i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>𝛒</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\bm{\rho}_{i}\bm{x}_{t-i}</annotation></semantics></math>, we employ <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> groups of heads, where group <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> contains <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> heads each of dimension. Given the model dimension <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\sum_{m=1}^{M}H_{m}\cdot d_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\sum_{m=1}^{M}H_{m}\cdot d_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, with probability at least <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.E6.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{D}(\bm{X})\leq\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\rho}_{m}\|_{2}B\left((1+\varepsilon_{\delta})\mathbb{I}_{\left\{d_{m}\leq d\right\}}\sqrt{1-\frac{d_{m}}{d}}+\frac{1.3\ e^{0.02m}}{H_{m}}\right)+\sum_{k=M+1}^{L}\|\bm{\rho}_{k}\|_{2}B\ ," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>{</mo><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.500em">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{D}(\bm{X})\leq\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\rho}_{m}\|_{2}B\left((1+\varepsilon_{\delta})\mathbb{I}_{\left\{d_{m}\leq d\right\}}\sqrt{1-\frac{d_{m}}{d}}+\frac{1.3\ e^{0.02m}}{H_{m}}\right)+\sum_{k=M+1}^{L}\|\bm{\rho}_{k}\|_{2}B\ ,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A3.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\delta}=\sqrt{\frac{2\log{(2ML/\delta)}}{\min_{m}d_{m}}}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\delta}=\sqrt{\frac{2\log{(2ML/\delta)}}{\min_{m}d_{m}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and the first term in equation (<a href="#S4.E1" title="In Theorem 4.1. ‣ Linear sequence modeling. ‣ 4 Parameter trade-offs in Information Extraction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>) takes zero when <math id="A3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{m}&gt;d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{m}&gt;d</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A3.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">We only consider the case <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{m}\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{m}\leq d</annotation></semantics></math> in our proof, since otherwise there is no information loss and the first term in the approximation error vanishes. Since we only use a single layer of the Transformer, we omit the layer index.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Embedding layer.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We embed each token by</p>
<table id="A3.Ex29" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{E}=\begin{pmatrix}\bm{I}_{d}\\
\bm{0}_{(D-d)\times d}\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times d},\quad\bm{b}_{E}=\bm{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mi>d</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{E}=\begin{pmatrix}\bm{I}_{d}\\
\bm{0}_{(D-d)\times d}\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times d},\quad\bm{b}_{E}=\bm{0}\in\mathbb{R}^{D},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, then each token <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}^{(0)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}^{(0)}</annotation></semantics></math> after embedding is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}^{(0)}=\bm{W}_{E}\bm{x}_{t}+\bm{b}_{E}=\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{x}}_{t}\\
\bm{0}\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>E</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>𝒃</mi><mi>E</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>𝟎</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>D</mi></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}^{(0)}=\bm{W}_{E}\bm{x}_{t}+\bm{b}_{E}=\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{x}}_{t}\\
\bm{0}\end{pmatrix}\in\mathbb{R}^{D}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Multi-head attention layer with residual connection.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We implement multi-head attention using <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> groups of heads. Each group <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> comprises <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> heads with dimension <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(m=1,2,\ldots,M)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(m=1,2,\ldots,M)</annotation></semantics></math>, aimed at extracting the corresponding representation <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}</annotation></semantics></math> which is <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{x}}_{t-m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{x}}_{t-m}</annotation></semantics></math> after projection to <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>-dimension space.
This step can be presented as follows for each token:</p>
<table id="A3.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{x}}_{t}\\
0\\
\vdots\\
0\end{pmatrix}\longrightarrow\begin{pmatrix}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\\
\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-1}\\
\vdots\\
\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-M}\\
\bm{0}_{D-(\sum_{m=1}^{M}d_{m})}\end{pmatrix}:=\bm{x}_{t}^{(1/2)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}{\bm{x}}_{t}\\
0\\
\vdots\\
0\end{pmatrix}\longrightarrow\begin{pmatrix}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\\
\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-1}\\
\vdots\\
\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-M}\\
\bm{0}_{D-(\sum_{m=1}^{M}d_{m})}\end{pmatrix}:=\bm{x}_{t}^{(1/2)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is obtained by residual connection.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We now focus on the extraction of an arbitrary <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}</annotation></semantics></math> and give the details of construction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">By lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma1" title="Lemma B.1. ‣ Appendix B Lemmas used in Proofs ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a>, for any rate <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q\in\mathbb{N}^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>q</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q\in\mathbb{N}^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a function</p>
<table id="A3.Ex32" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex32.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{m}^{\exp}(t)=\sum_{h=1}^{H_{m}}\alpha_{h,m}e^{-\beta_{h,m}(t-1)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>exp</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{m}^{\exp}(t)=\sum_{h=1}^{H_{m}}\alpha_{h,m}e^{-\beta_{h,m}(t-1)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.2" class="ltx_p">such that <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{h}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{h}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and</p>
<table id="A3.Ex33" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex33.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\|\mathbb{I}\left(\cdot=m\right)-\phi_{m}^{\exp}(\cdot)\|_{\ell_{1}(\mathbb{N})}=\sum_{s=0}^{+\infty}|\mathbb{I}\left(s=m\right)-\phi^{\exp}(s)|\leq\frac{1.3\ e^{0.02m}}{H_{m}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>exp</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em" rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munderover><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>exp</mi></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0.167em">≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathbb{I}\left(\cdot=m\right)-\phi_{m}^{\exp}(\cdot)\|_{\ell_{1}(\mathbb{N})}=\sum_{s=0}^{+\infty}|\mathbb{I}\left(s=m\right)-\phi^{\exp}(s)|\leq\frac{1.3\ e^{0.02m}}{H_{m}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma B.2 (High-probability projection). ‣ Appendix B Lemmas used in Proofs ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, there exist an projection <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{P}_{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{m}\times d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{P}_{m}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{m}\times d}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A3.Ex34" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex34.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr\Big[\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}_{m}^{\top}\bm{P}_{m})\bm{x}_{l}\|_{2}\geq B\sqrt{1-\frac{d_{m}}{d}}\,(1+\varepsilon)\Big]\leq 2\exp\Big(-\frac{d_{m}\varepsilon^{2}}{2}\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑰</mi><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>m</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">≥</mo><mi>B</mi><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msqrt><mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>exp</mi><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr\Big[\|(\bm{I}-\bm{P}_{m}^{\top}\bm{P}_{m})\bm{x}_{l}\|_{2}\geq B\sqrt{1-\frac{d_{m}}{d}}\,(1+\varepsilon)\Big]\leq 2\exp\Big(-\frac{d_{m}\varepsilon^{2}}{2}\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.2" class="ltx_p">for any <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l=1,\ldots,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l=1,\ldots,L</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}:=\bm{P}_{m}\bm{x}_{t-m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}:=\bm{P}_{m}\bm{x}_{t-m}</annotation></semantics></math>
For <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h=\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}H_{i},\ \sum_{j=1}^{m-1}H_{j}+1\ ,\ldots,\ \sum_{k=1}^{m}H_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.500em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.500em">,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo rspace="0.500em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h=\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}H_{i},\ \sum_{j=1}^{m-1}H_{j}+1\ ,\ldots,\ \sum_{k=1}^{m}H_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, we choose parameters as follows</p>
<table id="A3.Ex35" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex35.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{(h)}=\beta_{h,m},\quad\bm{W}_{V}^{(h)}=\alpha_{h,m}\left(\sum_{i=0}^{H_{m}}\exp(-\beta_{h,m}(i-1))\right)\bm{P}_{m},\quad\bm{W}_{K}^{(h)}=\bm{W}_{Q}^{(h)}={0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>V</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></munderover><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>K</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{(h)}=\beta_{h,m},\quad\bm{W}_{V}^{(h)}=\alpha_{h,m}\left(\sum_{i=0}^{H_{m}}\exp(-\beta_{h,m}(i-1))\right)\bm{P}_{m},\quad\bm{W}_{K}^{(h)}=\bm{W}_{Q}^{(h)}={0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.1" class="ltx_p">The output of <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> heads are concatenated together, and we take</p>
<table id="A3.Ex36" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex36.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{W}_{O}=\sum_{m=1}^{M}\sum_{h=\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}H_{i}+1}^{\sum_{j=1}^{m}H_{j}}\bm{S}_{m,h}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>O</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{W}_{O}=\sum_{m=1}^{M}\sum_{h=\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}H_{i}+1}^{\sum_{j=1}^{m}H_{j}}\bm{S}_{m,h},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{S}_{m,h}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{S}_{m,h}\in\mathbb{R}^{D\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> moves the output of the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m-" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m-</annotation></semantics></math>th set of heads to the same position</p>
<table id="A3.Ex37" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex37.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{S}_{m,h}=\begin{pmatrix}\bm{0}_{(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i})\times(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}+(h-1)d_{m})}&amp;\bm{0}_{(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i})\times d_{m}}&amp;\bm{0}_{(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i})\times(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}-hd_{m})}\\
\\
\bm{0}_{d_{m}\times(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}+(h-1)d_{m})}&amp;\bm{I}_{d_{m}\times d_{m}}&amp;\bm{0}_{d_{m}\times(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}-hd_{m})}\\
\\
\bm{0}_{(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m}d_{m})\times(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}+(h-1)d_{m})}&amp;\bm{0}_{(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m}d_{m})\times d_{m}}&amp;\bm{0}_{(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m}d_{m})\times(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}-hd_{m})}\end{pmatrix}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝑺</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>𝑰</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mtd><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{S}_{m,h}=\begin{pmatrix}\bm{0}_{(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i})\times(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}+(h-1)d_{m})}&amp;\bm{0}_{(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i})\times d_{m}}&amp;\bm{0}_{(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i})\times(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}-hd_{m})}\\
\\
\bm{0}_{d_{m}\times(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}+(h-1)d_{m})}&amp;\bm{I}_{d_{m}\times d_{m}}&amp;\bm{0}_{d_{m}\times(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}-hd_{m})}\\
\\
\bm{0}_{(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m}d_{m})\times(\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}+(h-1)d_{m})}&amp;\bm{0}_{(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m}d_{m})\times d_{m}}&amp;\bm{0}_{(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m}d_{m})\times(D-\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}d_{i}-hd_{m})}\end{pmatrix}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We define</p>
<table id="A3.Ex38" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex38.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\bm{P}}_{m}:=\left(0_{d_{H}\times(m-1)d_{H}},I_{d_{m}\times d_{m}},0_{d_{H}\times(D-md_{H})}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{m}\times D},\quad m\in[M]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>I</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mn>0</mn><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>M</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\bm{P}}_{m}:=\left(0_{d_{H}\times(m-1)d_{H}},I_{d_{m}\times d_{m}},0_{d_{H}\times(D-md_{H})}\right)\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{m}\times D},\quad m\in[M],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">then</p>
<table id="A3.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex39"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex39.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\tilde{\bm{P}}_{m}\cdot\mathrm{Concat}\bigg(\mathrm{Attn}^{(h)}(\bm{X}^{(0)})\bigg)_{h=1}^{H}=\sum_{h=\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}H_{i}}^{\sum_{j=1}^{m}H_{j}}\alpha_{h,m}\sum_{s=1}^{\infty}e^{-\beta_{h,m}(s-1)}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-s}:=\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑷</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>Concat</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Attn</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>h</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>H</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msubsup><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>m</mi></msubsup></mstyle><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mrow><mi>h</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\tilde{\bm{P}}_{m}\cdot\mathrm{Concat}\bigg(\mathrm{Attn}^{(h)}(\bm{X}^{(0)})\bigg)_{h=1}^{H}=\sum_{h=\sum_{i=1}^{m-1}H_{i}}^{\sum_{j=1}^{m}H_{j}}\alpha_{h,m}\sum_{s=1}^{\infty}e^{-\beta_{h,m}(s-1)}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-s}:=\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px2.p7.1" class="ltx_p">And the approximation error of this step is</p>
<table id="A3.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex40"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>Attn</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex40.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{t}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\left\|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}-\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}\right\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{t}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\left\|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}-\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}\right\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex41"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex41.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\sup_{t}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\mathbb{I}\left(\cdot=m\right)-\phi_{m}^{\exp}(\cdot)\|_{\ell_{1}(\mathbb{N})}\cdot B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>t</mi></munder><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em">=</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>exp</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sup_{t}\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\mathbb{I}\left(\cdot=m\right)-\phi_{m}^{\exp}(\cdot)\|_{\ell_{1}(\mathbb{N})}\cdot B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex42"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex42.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B\cdot\sum_{m=1}^{M}\frac{1.3\ e^{0.02m}}{H_{m}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.500em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B\cdot\sum_{m=1}^{M}\frac{1.3\ e^{0.02m}}{H_{m}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Feed forward network.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">FFN is implemented component-wise to realize convolution. The final output for the <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th token is</p>
<table id="A3.Ex43" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex43.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{m=0}^{M}\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{m=0}^{M}\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}=\bm{\rho}_{m}{\bm{P}_{m}}^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mmultiscripts><mi>𝑷</mi><mi>m</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}=\bm{\rho}_{m}{\bm{P}_{m}}^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>. In fact we only need a linear map to achieve this, and FFN won’t cause any approximation error.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Approximation error.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma B.2 (High-probability projection). ‣ Appendix B Lemmas used in Proofs ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, with probability at least
<math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-M\max_{m}2\exp\Big(-\frac{d_{m}\varepsilon^{2}}{2}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-M\max_{m}2\exp\Big(-\frac{d_{m}\varepsilon^{2}}{2}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
</div>
<div id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A3.Ex44" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A3.Ex44X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{D}(\bm{X})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{D}(\bm{X})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\bm{{\rho}}_{m}{\bm{x}}_{t-m}-\sum_{m=0}^{M}\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\sum_{m=0}^{\infty}\bm{{\rho}}_{m}{\bm{x}}_{t-m}-\sum_{m=0}^{M}\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex44Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\rho}_{m}\bm{x}_{t-m}-\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}\|_{2}+\sum_{k=M+1}^{\infty}\|\bm{\rho}_{k}\|_{2}B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\rho}_{m}\bm{x}_{t-m}-\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}\|_{2}+\sum_{k=M+1}^{\infty}\|\bm{\rho}_{k}\|_{2}B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex44Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\rho}_{m}\bm{x}_{t-m}-\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}\|_{2}+\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\tilde{\bm{\rho}}_{m}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}-\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}\|_{2}+\sum_{k=M+1}^{\infty}\|\bm{\rho}_{k}\|_{2}B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝝆</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\rho}_{m}\bm{x}_{t-m}-\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}\|_{2}+\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\tilde{\bm{\rho}}_{m}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-m}-\bm{\tilde{\rho}}_{m}\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-m}\|_{2}+\sum_{k=M+1}^{\infty}\|\bm{\rho}_{k}\|_{2}B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A3.Ex44Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{(By Lemma \ref{lemma: prob projection} )}\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mtext>(By Lemma </mtext><mtext><a href="#A2.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma B.2 (High-probability projection). ‣ Appendix B Lemmas used in Proofs ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a></mtext><mtext> )</mtext></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{(By Lemma \ref{lemma: prob projection} )}\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A3.Ex44Xc.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle B\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\rho}_{m}\|_{2}\left(\sqrt{1-\frac{d_{m}}{d}}(1+\varepsilon)+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}}\right)+B\sum_{k=M+1}^{\infty}\|\bm{\rho}_{k}\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>Attn</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle B\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\rho}_{m}\|_{2}\left(\sqrt{1-\frac{d_{m}}{d}}(1+\varepsilon)+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}}\right)+B\sum_{k=M+1}^{\infty}\|\bm{\rho}_{k}\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Take uniform bound over <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>L</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">L</annotation></semantics></math> tokens, with probability at least <math id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="A3.Ex45" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A3.Ex45.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{D}(\bm{X})\leq\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\rho}_{m}\|_{2}B\left(\sqrt{1-\frac{d_{m}}{d}}\left(1+\sqrt{\frac{2\log{(2ML/\delta)}}{\min_{m}d_{m}}}\right)+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}}\right)+\sum_{k=M+1}^{\infty}\|\bm{\rho}_{k}\|_{2}B" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>d</mi></mfrac></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>Attn</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝆</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{D}(\bm{X})\leq\sum_{m=1}^{M}\|\bm{\rho}_{m}\|_{2}B\left(\sqrt{1-\frac{d_{m}}{d}}\left(1+\sqrt{\frac{2\log{(2ML/\delta)}}{\min_{m}d_{m}}}\right)+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}}\right)+\sum_{k=M+1}^{\infty}\|\bm{\rho}_{k}\|_{2}B</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A3.SS0.SSS0.Px4.p2.2" class="ltx_p">∎</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A4" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix D </span>Proof of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (The saturation pattern of softmax). ‣ 5 Softmax Saturation and Parameter Reduction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 5.1. ‣ 5 Softmax Saturation and Parameter Reduction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a></h2>

<div id="A4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we prove Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (The saturation pattern of softmax). ‣ 5 Softmax Saturation and Parameter Reduction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> and Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 5.1. ‣ 5 Softmax Saturation and Parameter Reduction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, we first restate the results:</p>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restate of Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (The saturation pattern of softmax). ‣ 5 Softmax Saturation and Parameter Reduction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>)<span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Assume <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{Logits}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})\|_{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Logits</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{Logits}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})\|_{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded. Let <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{l}=\frac{\partial(\mathrm{AttnScore}_{d_{H}}\bm{e}_{l})}{\partial(\mathrm{Logits}_{d_{H}}\bm{e}_{l})}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>AttnScore</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Logits</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐞</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{l}=\frac{\partial(\mathrm{AttnScore}_{d_{H}}\bm{e}_{l})}{\partial(\mathrm{Logits}_{d_{H}}\bm{e}_{l})}</annotation></semantics></math> be the column-wise Jacobian for <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math>. Then we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex46" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex46.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\left\|J_{l}\right\|_{2}=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{L}\right),\quad l=1,2,\ldots,L," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mi>l</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|J_{l}\right\|_{2}=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{1}{L}\right),\quad l=1,2,\ldots,L,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> hides an absolute constant depends on <math id="A4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Logits}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Logits</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Logits}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A4.Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary D.1</span></span><span id="A4.Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Restatement of Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 5.1. ‣ 5 Softmax Saturation and Parameter Reduction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>)<span id="A4.Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same condition as Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (The saturation pattern of softmax). ‣ 5 Softmax Saturation and Parameter Reduction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, for any <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{AttnScore}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>AttnScore</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{AttnScore}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{h}\leq d_{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{h}\leq d_{H}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exist <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\bm{W}}_{K},\hat{\bm{W}}_{Q}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}\times D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐖</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\bm{W}}_{K},\hat{\bm{W}}_{Q}\in\mathbb{R}^{d_{h}\times D}</annotation></semantics></math> such that for any <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l\in[L]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>L</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l\in[L]</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="A4.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|(\mathrm{AttnScore}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})-\mathrm{AttnScore}_{d_{h}}(\hat{\bm{W}}_{Q},\hat{\bm{W}}_{K},\bm{X}))\bm{e}_{l}\right\|_{2}=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{\Lambda_{h}^{H}}{L}\right)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>AttnScore</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>AttnScore</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒆</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mi>L</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|(\mathrm{AttnScore}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})-\mathrm{AttnScore}_{d_{h}}(\hat{\bm{W}}_{Q},\hat{\bm{W}}_{K},\bm{X}))\bm{e}_{l}\right\|_{2}=\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{\Lambda_{h}^{H}}{L}\right),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Lambda_{h}^{H}=\sum_{i=d_{h}+1}^{d_{H}}\sigma({\bm{W}_{Q}^{T}}^{\top}\bm{W}_{K}^{T})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi mathvariant="normal">Λ</mi><mi>h</mi><mi>H</mi></msubsup><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>h</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msubsup><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi><mi>T</mi><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Lambda_{h}^{H}=\sum_{i=d_{h}+1}^{d_{H}}\sigma({\bm{W}_{Q}^{T}}^{\top}\bm{W}_{K}^{T})</annotation></semantics></math> is the tail sum of singular values of original logits matrices, and <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}</annotation></semantics></math> hides an absolute constant depends on <math id="A4.Thmcorollary1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Logits}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Logits</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>𝐖</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Logits}_{d_{H}}(\bm{W}_{Q},\bm{W}_{K},\bm{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A4.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, we focus on a certain index <math id="A4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>. For simplicity of notation, we let <math id="A4.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝒛</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{z}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the <math id="A4.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math>-th column of <math id="A4.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigg&lt;\bm{W}_{Q}\bm{X},\bm{W}_{K}\bm{X}\bigg&gt;+\bm{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo fence="false" mathsize="2.100em">⟨</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>Q</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>K</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo fence="false" mathsize="2.100em">⟩</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>𝑹</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigg&lt;\bm{W}_{Q}\bm{X},\bm{W}_{K}\bm{X}\bigg&gt;+\bm{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and denote <math id="A4.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{softmax}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>softmax</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{softmax}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="A4.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>σ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma</annotation></semantics></math>, and the <math id="A4.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>-th component of output vector as <math id="A4.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Through direct computation, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex47" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A4.Ex47X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A4.Ex47X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J\sigma(\bm{z})=diag(\sigma(\bm{z}))-\sigma(\bm{z})\sigma(\bm{z})^{\top}=\begin{cases}\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})^{2},&amp;i=j,\\
-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})\sigma_{j}(\bm{z}),&amp;i\neq j.\end{cases}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J\sigma(\bm{z})=diag(\sigma(\bm{z}))-\sigma(\bm{z})\sigma(\bm{z})^{\top}=\begin{cases}\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})^{2},&amp;i=j,\\
-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})\sigma_{j}(\bm{z}),&amp;i\neq j.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text">And notice that <math id="A4.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\sigma(\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\sigma(\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math> is semidefinite. In fact, let <math id="A4.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=\sigma(\bm{z})\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=\sigma(\bm{z})\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, so that <math id="A4.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A4.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i=1}^{L}p_{i}=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i=1}^{L}p_{i}=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A4.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v\in\mathbb{R}^{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>L</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v\in\mathbb{R}^{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, we compute the quadratic form:</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex48" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex48.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}J\sigma(\bm{z})v=v^{\top}\big(\mathrm{diag}(p)-pp^{\top}\big)v=\sum_{i=1}^{L}p_{i}v_{i}^{2}-\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{L}p_{i}v_{i}\Big)^{2}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>diag</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}J\sigma(\bm{z})v=v^{\top}\big(\mathrm{diag}(p)-pp^{\top}\big)v=\sum_{i=1}^{L}p_{i}v_{i}^{2}-\Big(\sum_{i=1}^{L}p_{i}v_{i}\Big)^{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">The right-hand side is exactly the variance of the random variable <math id="A4.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>V</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V</annotation></semantics></math> taking values <math id="A4.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>v</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> with probability <math id="A4.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e.</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex49" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex49.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="v^{\top}J\sigma(\bm{z})v=\mathbb{E}_{p}[V^{2}]-\big(\mathbb{E}_{p}[V]\big)^{2}=\mathrm{Var}_{p}(V)\,\geq 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>v</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>V</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>Var</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>V</mi><mo rspace="0.170em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">v^{\top}J\sigma(\bm{z})v=\mathbb{E}_{p}[V^{2}]-\big(\mathbb{E}_{p}[V]\big)^{2}=\mathrm{Var}_{p}(V)\,\geq 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore <math id="A4.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\sigma(\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\sigma(\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math> is positive semidefinite.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">According to Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma4" title="Lemma B.4 (Gershgorin circle theorem). ‣ Appendix B Lemmas used in Proofs ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>, for an eigenvalue <math id="A4.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A4.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J\sigma(\bm{z})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J\sigma(\bm{z})</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an <math id="A4.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math> such that</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex50" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex50.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|\lambda-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})(1-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z}))|\leq\sum_{j\neq i}\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})\sigma_{j}(\bm{z})=\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})(1-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z}))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|\lambda-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})(1-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z}))|\leq\sum_{j\neq i}\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})\sigma_{j}(\bm{z})=\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})(1-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A4.p5.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p5.2.1" class="ltx_text">Hence, <math id="A4.p5.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0\leq\lambda\leq\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>λ</mi><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0\leq\lambda\leq\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text">Since the sum of the eigenvalues of a matrix is equal to its trace, we have</span></p>
<table id="A4.Ex51" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A4.Ex51.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\leq\sum_{i}\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})(1-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z}))\leq 1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mi>i</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sum_{i}\lambda_{i}\leq\sum_{i}\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})(1-\sigma_{i}(\bm{z}))\leq 1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A4.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma3" title="Lemma B.3. ‣ Appendix B Lemmas used in Proofs ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>, <math id="A4.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})\sim\frac{1}{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{i}(\bm{z})\sim\frac{1}{L}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A4.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda_{i}\sim\frac{1}{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda_{i}\sim\frac{1}{L}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A4.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=1,2,\ldots,L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=1,2,\ldots,L</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="A4.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|J\sigma(\bm{z})\|\sim\frac{1}{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒛</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>L</mi></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|J\sigma(\bm{z})\|\sim\frac{1}{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A4.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">To prove Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 5.1. ‣ 5 Softmax Saturation and Parameter Reduction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>, we take <math id="A4.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\hat{\bm{W}}_{Q}}^{\top}\hat{\bm{W}}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>Q</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\hat{\bm{W}}_{Q}}^{\top}\hat{\bm{W}}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math> as the low-rank approximation of <math id="A4.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{W}_{Q}}^{\top}\bm{W}_{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mmultiscripts><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>Q</mi><mrow></mrow><mrow></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></mmultiscripts><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝑾</mi><mi>K</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{W}_{Q}}^{\top}\bm{W}_{K}</annotation></semantics></math>. then Corollary <a href="#S5.Thmcorollary1" title="Corollary 5.1. ‣ 5 Softmax Saturation and Parameter Reduction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> can be dirctectly obtained from Theorem <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 5.1 (The saturation pattern of softmax). ‣ 5 Softmax Saturation and Parameter Reduction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a> and Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma5" title="Lemma B.5 (Mean Value Inequality for vector-valued functions). ‣ Appendix B Lemmas used in Proofs ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A4.p9" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A4.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A4.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A5" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix E </span>Approximation and tradeoff results for nonlinear target</h2>

<section id="A5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.1 </span>Induction Head</h3>

<div id="A5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib67" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang et al. (2025)</a></cite> defined a generalized induction head:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex52" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex52.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{IH}_{n:t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{s=n}^{t-1}\pi_{s}\bm{x}_{s}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>IH</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{IH}_{n:t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{s=n}^{t-1}\pi_{s}\bm{x}_{s},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where</p>
<table id="A5.Ex53" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex53.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\pi_{s}=\mathrm{softmax}\bigg(\left(\bm{X}_{t-n+2:t}\bm{W}^{*}\bm{X}_{v-n+1:v-1}\right)_{v=n}^{L-1}\bigg)_{v=s}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>softmax</mi><msub><mrow><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><msup><mi>𝑾</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo maxsize="2.100em" minsize="2.100em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>v</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{s}=\mathrm{softmax}\bigg(\left(\bm{X}_{t-n+2:t}\bm{W}^{*}\bm{X}_{v-n+1:v-1}\right)_{v=n}^{L-1}\bigg)_{v=s},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and empirically pointed out that the first Transformer layer is used to extract information. In fact, the parameter allocation problem for the first layer reduces to the <math id="A5.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>-gram case.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We systematically investigated the effect of Transformer architectural variants on the Induction Head task in Figure <a href="#A5.F7.fig1" title="Figure 7 ‣ E.1 Induction Head ‣ Appendix E Approximation and tradeoff results for nonlinear target ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>, which tests a model’s ability to recognize and extend repeated patterns—a fundamental reasoning mechanism for in-context learning. The task was constructed using synthetic sequences of length 128 with 10 unique tokens and embedded 5-token repeating patterns, yielding a dataset of 10,000 sequences (80%/20% train/validation).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">The model architecture was a two-layer Transformer encoder with <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}=256" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>256</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}=256</annotation></semantics></math>, pre-norm configuration, GELU feed-forward networks, learned positional encodings, and a two-layer MLP output head. We varied the number of attention heads in <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{1,2,4,8,16,32}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>32</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{1,2,4,8,16,32}</annotation></semantics></math> while keeping <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{\mathrm{model}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>model</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{\mathrm{model}}</annotation></semantics></math> fixed. Models were trained for 500 epochs using AdamW (learning rate <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\in{10^{-3},5!\times!10^{-4},10^{-4}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∈</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>5</mn><mo rspace="0.055em">!</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo>!</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mn>10</mn><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\in{10^{-3},5!\times!10^{-4},10^{-4}}</annotation></semantics></math>, weight decay <math id="A5.SS1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>4</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-4}</annotation></semantics></math>), cosine scheduling with ReduceLROnPlateau, gradient clipping (1.0), and mixed precision. Each configuration was repeated with three random seeds, and the best-performing model was selected by validation mean squared error (MSE).</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Evaluation included validation MSE, heatmaps of performance across architectural variants, and qualitative prediction analysis. The results reveal how the number of heads influences the ability of the model to capture the Induction Head mechanism and demonstrate the robustness of certain configurations across seeds. This provides practical guidance for architectural design in tasks requiring in-context learning.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A5.F7.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_middle" style="width:278.2pt;"><img src="2510.03784v1/exp_results/0_tradeoff/ih_tradeoff.png" id="A5.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:384/252;" width="384" height="252" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 7: </span>Induction Head Tradeoff</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">E.2 </span>Continuous Time-homogeneous System</h3>

<div id="A5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this subection, we analyze the approximation error of a continuous target function and derive the resulting trade-off.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We consider a sequence-to-sequence model in which both the input <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}=(\bm{x}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{Z}}\subset\mathcal{X}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}=(\bm{x}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{Z}}\subset\mathcal{X}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math> and output <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}=(\bm{y}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{Z}}\subset\mathcal{Y}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝒀</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}=(\bm{y}_{t})_{t\in\mathbb{Z}}\subset\mathcal{Y}\subset\mathbb{R}^{d\times\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math> are sequences of infinite length and input tokens <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are i.i.d. (we need a stronger assumption due to the target) random vectors with zero mean and identity covariance matrix and whose norm is bounded by <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>B</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B</annotation></semantics></math>.
<math id="A5.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{H}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the mapping from <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}=\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}=\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To give the mapping <math id="A5.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}</annotation></semantics></math> practical relevance, we must impose certain properties on the target function space. We now present the definitions of these properties.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{H}=\left\{\mathrm{H}_{t}:\mathcal{X}\mapsto\mathbb{R}^{d};t\in\mathbb{R}\right\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">↦</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo>;</mo><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}=\left\{\mathrm{H}_{t}:\mathcal{X}\mapsto\mathbb{R}^{d};t\in\mathbb{R}\right\}</annotation></semantics></math> be a sequence of functionals.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">1.(<span id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Linear</span>) <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is linear if for any <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda,\lambda^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda,\lambda^{\prime}\in\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X},\bm{X}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X},\bm{X}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\lambda\bm{X}+\lambda^{\prime}\bm{X}^{\prime})=\lambda\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})+\lambda\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mi>λ</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\lambda\bm{X}+\lambda^{\prime}\bm{X}^{\prime})=\lambda\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})+\lambda\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">2.(<span id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Continuous</span>) <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous if for any <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X},\bm{X}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X},\bm{X}^{\prime}\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{\bm{X}^{\prime}\rightarrow\bm{X}}|\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X}^{\prime})-\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})|=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{\bm{X}^{\prime}\rightarrow\bm{X}}|\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X}^{\prime})-\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})|=0</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">3.(<span id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Bounded</span>) <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is bounded if <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{\bm{X}\in\mathcal{X},\bm{X}\neq\bm{0}}\frac{|\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})|}{\|\bm{X}\|_{\infty}}\leq\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>≠</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow></mrow></msub><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msub></mfrac></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{\bm{X}\in\mathcal{X},\bm{X}\neq\bm{0}}\frac{|\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})|}{\|\bm{X}\|_{\infty}}\leq\infty</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">4.(<span id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Time-homogeneous</span>) <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}={\mathrm{H}_{t}:t\in\mathbb{R}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}={\mathrm{H}_{t}:t\in\mathbb{R}}</annotation></semantics></math> is time-homogeneous (or shift-equivariant) if the input-output relationship commutes with time shift: let <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[S_{\tau}(\bm{X})]_{t}=\bm{x}_{t-\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[S_{\tau}(\bm{X})]_{t}=\bm{x}_{t-\tau}</annotation></semantics></math> be a shift operator, then <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}(S_{\tau}\bm{X})=S_{\tau}\mathrm{H}(\bm{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>H</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝑿</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>τ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>H</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}(S_{\tau}\bm{X})=S_{\tau}\mathrm{H}(\bm{X})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">5.(<span id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Causal</span>) <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is causal if it does not depend on future values of the input. That is, if <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X},\bm{X}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X},\bm{X}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfy <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{t}=\bm{x}_{t}^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{t}=\bm{x}_{t}^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X}^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X}^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math> for any <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\leq t_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\leq t_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p7.1" class="ltx_p">6.(<span id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regular</span>) <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is regular if for any sequence <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{\bm{X}^{(n)}\in\mathcal{X}:n\in\mathbb{Z}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{\bm{X}^{(n)}\in\mathcal{X}:n\in\mathbb{Z}}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A5.Thmdefinition1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{(n)}_{t}\rightarrow\bm{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{(n)}_{t}\rightarrow\bm{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, then</p>
<table id="A5.Ex54" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex54.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X}^{(n)})=\bm{0}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{n\rightarrow\infty}\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X}^{(n)})=\bm{0}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p">According to the following lemma, the target we studied in Section <a href="#S4" title="4 Parameter trade-offs in Information Extraction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> is a continuous, linear, regular, causal and time-homogeneous functional.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}</annotation></semantics></math> be a family of continuous, linear, regular, causal and time-homogeneous functionals on <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then, there exist a sequence <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho:\mathbb{N}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho:\mathbb{N}\rightarrow\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> that is summable, i.e.</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex55" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex55.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\rho\|_{l^{1}}:=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}|(\rho_{i})_{j}|&lt;\infty" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi>l</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\rho\|_{l^{1}}:=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=0}^{\infty}|(\rho_{i})_{j}|&lt;\infty</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex56" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex56.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\rho_{i}\bm{x}_{t-i},\ t\in\mathbb{Z}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\rho_{i}\bm{x}_{t-i},\ t\in\mathbb{Z}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">In particular, <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H</annotation></semantics></math> is uniformly bounded with <math id="A5.Thmlemma1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{t}\|H_{t}\|=\|\rho\|_{\ell^{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{t}\|H_{t}\|=\|\rho\|_{\ell^{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text">We prove the existence of a summable sequence <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>ℕ</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho:\mathbb{N}\to\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying the stated properties. Let <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}=\ell^{\infty}(\mathbb{Z};\mathbb{R}^{d})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ℤ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}=\ell^{\infty}(\mathbb{Z};\mathbb{R}^{d})</annotation></semantics></math> with the sup-norm <math id="A5.SS2.p5.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{X}\|=\sup_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\max_{1\leq i\leq d}|X_{k,i}|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{X}\|=\sup_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\max_{1\leq i\leq d}|X_{k,i}|</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Riesz representation and causality.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">Since each <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> is continuous, linear, and regular, by the Riesz representation theorem for <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\ell^{\infty}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\ell^{\infty}</annotation></semantics></math> spaces with regular functionals, there exists a unique <span id="A5.SS2.p6.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">finitely additive</span> signed vector measure <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ℤ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math> such that</p>
<table id="A5.Ex57" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex57.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\int_{\mathbb{Z}}\bm{X}^{T}d\bm{\mu}_{t}=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\bm{X}_{k}^{T}\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{k\})," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></msub><mrow><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>T</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\int_{\mathbb{Z}}\bm{X}^{T}d\bm{\mu}_{t}=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\bm{X}_{k}^{T}\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{k\}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p6.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{k\})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mi>d</mi></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{k\})\in\mathbb{R}^{d}</annotation></semantics></math> is the mass at integer <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.SS2.p6.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|H_{t}\|=\|\bm{\mu}_{t}\|=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\sum_{i=1}^{d}|\mu_{t,i}(\{k\})|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|H_{t}\|=\|\bm{\mu}_{t}\|=\sum_{k\in\mathbb{Z}}\sum_{i=1}^{d}|\mu_{t,i}(\{k\})|</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">Causality implies that <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})</annotation></semantics></math> depends only on <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\bm{X}_{k}:k\leq t\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\bm{X}_{k}:k\leq t\}</annotation></semantics></math>. Hence, <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{k\})=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{k\})=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="A5.SS2.p7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;t</annotation></semantics></math>, and the representation simplifies to:</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex58" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex58.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{k=-\infty}^{t}\bm{X}_{k}^{T}\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{k\})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{k=-\infty}^{t}\bm{X}_{k}^{T}\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{k\}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Time homogeneity and shift invariance.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">For any <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, time homogeneity implies <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\mathrm{H}_{t+\tau}(\bm{X}^{(\tau)})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\mathrm{H}_{t+\tau}(\bm{X}^{(\tau)})</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}^{(\tau)}_{k}=\bm{X}_{k-\tau}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}^{(\tau)}_{k}=\bm{X}_{k-\tau}</annotation></semantics></math>. Applying (1) to the right-hand side:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex59" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex59.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t+\tau}(\bm{X}^{(\tau)})=\sum_{m=-\infty}^{t+\tau}\bm{X}_{m-\tau}^{T}\bm{\mu}_{t+\tau}(\{m\})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>m</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t+\tau}(\bm{X}^{(\tau)})=\sum_{m=-\infty}^{t+\tau}\bm{X}_{m-\tau}^{T}\bm{\mu}_{t+\tau}(\{m\}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.2" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A5.SS2.p8.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="j=m-\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">j=m-\tau</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex60" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex60.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t+\tau}(\bm{X}^{(\tau)})=\sum_{j=-\infty}^{t}\bm{X}_{j}^{T}\bm{\mu}_{t+\tau}(\{j+\tau\})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mi>j</mi><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t+\tau}(\bm{X}^{(\tau)})=\sum_{j=-\infty}^{t}\bm{X}_{j}^{T}\bm{\mu}_{t+\tau}(\{j+\tau\}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p8.3" class="ltx_p">Equating with (1) and comparing coefficients:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex61" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex61.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{j\})=\bm{\mu}_{t+\tau}(\{j+\tau\})\quad\forall j\leq t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>τ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{j\})=\bm{\mu}_{t+\tau}(\{j+\tau\})\quad\forall j\leq t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p9.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Construction of <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ρ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho</annotation></semantics></math>.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">Fix <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=0</annotation></semantics></math> in (2) and set <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau=-t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau=-t</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex62" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex62.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{j\})=\bm{\mu}_{0}(\{j+t\})\quad\forall j\leq t." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mspace style="width:1.167em;" width="1.167em"></mspace><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∀</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}_{t}(\{j\})=\bm{\mu}_{0}(\{j+t\})\quad\forall j\leq t.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p9.2" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}(\{k\})=\bm{\mu}_{0}(\{k\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝝁</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}(\{k\})=\bm{\mu}_{0}(\{k\})</annotation></semantics></math>. By causality, <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{\mu}(\{k\})=\mathbf{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>𝟎</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{\mu}(\{k\})=\mathbf{0}</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>. Using time homogeneity:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex63" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex63.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\mathrm{H}_{0}(\bm{X}^{(-t)})=\sum_{k=-\infty}^{0}\bm{X}_{k+t}^{T}\bm{\mu}(\{k\})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\mathrm{H}_{0}(\bm{X}^{(-t)})=\sum_{k=-\infty}^{0}\bm{X}_{k+t}^{T}\bm{\mu}(\{k\}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p9.3" class="ltx_p">Substituting <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i=-k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i=-k</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex64" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex64.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\bm{X}_{t-i}^{T}\bm{\mu}(\{-i\})." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝑿</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\bm{X}_{t-i}^{T}\bm{\mu}(\{-i\}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p9.4" class="ltx_p">Define <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\rho_{i}=\bm{\mu}(\{-i\})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝝁</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\rho_{i}=\bm{\mu}(\{-i\})</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="A5.SS2.p9.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Then (3) becomes:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex65" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex65.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\bm{x}_{t-i}^{T}\rho_{i}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>T</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\bm{x}_{t-i}^{T}\rho_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4: Summability and norm equality.</span> 
<br class="ltx_break">From the Riesz representation and causality:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex66" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex66.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\rho\|_{\ell^{1}}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|(\rho_{i})_{j}|=\sum_{k=-\infty}^{0}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|\mu_{j}(\{k\})|=\|\bm{\mu}\|=\|H_{0}\|&lt;\infty." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>ρ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\rho\|_{\ell^{1}}=\sum_{i=0}^{\infty}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|(\rho_{i})_{j}|=\sum_{k=-\infty}^{0}\sum_{j=1}^{d}|\mu_{j}(\{k\})|=\|\bm{\mu}\|=\|H_{0}\|&lt;\infty.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p10.2" class="ltx_p">For any <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in\mathbb{Z}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in\mathbb{Z}</annotation></semantics></math>, using (2) and shift invariance:</p>
<table id="A5.Ex67" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex67.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\mathrm{H}_{t}\|=\sum_{j=-\infty}^{t}\sum_{i=1}^{d}|\mu_{t,i}(\{j\})|=\sum_{j=-\infty}^{t}\sum_{i=1}^{d}|\mu_{i}(\{j+t\})|=\|\bm{\mu}\|=\|\rho\|_{\ell^{1}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></munderover><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝝁</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\mathrm{H}_{t}\|=\sum_{j=-\infty}^{t}\sum_{i=1}^{d}|\mu_{t,i}(\{j\})|=\sum_{j=-\infty}^{t}\sum_{i=1}^{d}|\mu_{i}(\{j+t\})|=\|\bm{\mu}\|=\|\rho\|_{\ell^{1}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p10.3" class="ltx_p">Thus <math id="A5.SS2.p10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{t\in\mathbb{Z}}\|\mathrm{H}_{t}\|=\|\rho\|_{\ell^{1}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>sup</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>ℤ</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">ℓ</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{t\in\mathbb{Z}}\|\mathrm{H}_{t}\|=\|\rho\|_{\ell^{1}}</annotation></semantics></math>.
∎</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">We now consider a continuous time-homogeneous system. According to Theorem C.6 in <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib68" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wang &amp; Li (2023)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">de Figueiredo (1982)</a></cite>, we obtain the following decomposition result for such systems:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Volterra Series Decomposition)<span id="A5.Thmlemma2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> is a continuous time-homogeneous system with input <math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐗</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{X}</annotation></semantics></math> and output <math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐘</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, then <math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}</annotation></semantics></math> can be expanded in the Volterra series as follows</span></p>
<table id="A5.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.E8.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\bm{y}_{t}=\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=h_{0}+\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{\infty}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{\infty}\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝒚</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>h</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo rspace="0.055em">+</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></munderover><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{y}_{t}=\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=h_{0}+\sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{\infty}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{\infty}\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where <math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\otimes" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊗</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\otimes</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the Kronecker product. In particular, we call the expansion order <math id="A5.Thmlemma2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> to be the series’ order.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p">We focus on the term <math id="A5.SS2.p12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{H}^{(n)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}^{(n)}</annotation></semantics></math> and derive its approximation error when using a single-layer Transformer to approximate it. We begin by stating the lemmas required for our analysis:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma3" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.3</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{x_{i}\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> be i.i.d. random variables with <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[x_{i}]=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[x_{i}]=0</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[x_{i}^{2}]=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[x_{i}^{2}]=1</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then <math id="A5.Thmlemma3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigotimes_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigotimes_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is a random vector with mean zero and identity covariance matrix.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.3" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p13" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p13.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p13.1.1" class="ltx_text">It suffices to consider the scalar case <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d=1</annotation></semantics></math>. Define <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y:=\prod_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">:=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y:=\prod_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex68" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex68.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[y]=\mathbb{E}\left[\prod_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}\right]=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[x_{i}]=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[y]=\mathbb{E}\left[\prod_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}\right]=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[x_{i}]=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p13.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p13.2.1" class="ltx_text">and</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex69" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex69.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}[y^{2}]=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\prod_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}\right)^{2}\right]=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[x_{i}^{2}]=1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}[y^{2}]=\mathbb{E}\left[\left(\prod_{i=1}^{n}x_{i}\right)^{2}\right]=\prod_{i=1}^{n}\mathbb{E}[x_{i}^{2}]=1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p13.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p13.3.1" class="ltx_text">Thus <math id="A5.SS2.p13.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{Var}(y)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>Var</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Var}(y)=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which proves the claim.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma4" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.4</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bm{x}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bm{x}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic"> are random vectors with <math id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\bm{x}_{i}\|_{2}=B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\bm{x}_{i}\|_{2}=B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\bm{x}_{i}-\bar{\bm{x}}_{i}\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon_{i}\leq\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\bm{x}_{i}-\bar{\bm{x}}_{i}\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon_{i}\leq\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>. Then <math id="A5.Thmlemma4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{E}\|\bigotimes_{i=1}^{n}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{i}-\bigotimes_{i=1}^{n}\hat{\bm{x}}_{i}\|_{2}\leq\prod_{i=1}^{n}(B_{i}+\varepsilon_{i})-\prod_{i=1}^{n}B_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em">⨂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>⨂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝐱</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em">−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{E}\|\bigotimes_{i=1}^{n}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{i}-\bigotimes_{i=1}^{n}\hat{\bm{x}}_{i}\|_{2}\leq\prod_{i=1}^{n}(B_{i}+\varepsilon_{i})-\prod_{i=1}^{n}B_{i}</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.4" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p14" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p14.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p14.1.1" class="ltx_text">From the property of projection operation,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex70" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex70.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{i}-\hat{\bm{x}}_{i}\|_{2}\leq\|P\|_{2}\|\bm{x}_{i}-\hat{\bm{x}}_{i}\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon_{i}\leq\varepsilon." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>P</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|\tilde{\bm{x}}_{i}-\hat{\bm{x}}_{i}\|_{2}\leq\|P\|_{2}\|\bm{x}_{i}-\hat{\bm{x}}_{i}\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon_{i}\leq\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p14.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p14.2.1" class="ltx_text">By direct calculation,</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex71" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex71X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex71X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\|\bigotimes_{i=1}^{n}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{i}-\bigotimes_{i=1}^{n}\hat{\bm{x}}_{i}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">⨂</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathbb{E}\|\bigotimes_{i=1}^{n}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{i}-\bigotimes_{i=1}^{n}\hat{\bm{x}}_{i}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex71X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq\sum_{\phi\neq S\subset\{1,\ldots,n\}}\left(\prod_{i\in S}\varepsilon_{i}\right)\mathbb{E}\|\bigotimes_{j\notin S}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{j}\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">⨂</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq\sum_{\phi\neq S\subset\{1,\ldots,n\}}\left(\prod_{i\in S}\varepsilon_{i}\right)\mathbb{E}\|\bigotimes_{j\notin S}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{j}\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex71Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex71Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sum_{\phi\neq S\subset\{1,\ldots,n\}}\left(\prod_{i\in S}\varepsilon_{i}\right)\prod_{j\notin S}B_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>≠</mo><mi>S</mi><mo>⊂</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>∉</mo><mi>S</mi></mrow></munder></mstyle><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sum_{\phi\neq S\subset\{1,\ldots,n\}}\left(\prod_{i\in S}\varepsilon_{i}\right)\prod_{j\notin S}B_{j}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex71Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex71Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\prod_{i=1}^{n}(B_{i}+\varepsilon_{i})-\prod_{i=1}^{n}B_{i}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\prod_{i=1}^{n}(B_{i}+\varepsilon_{i})-\prod_{i=1}^{n}B_{i}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.SS2.p14.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p14.3.1" class="ltx_text">∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p15" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p15.1" class="ltx_p">We use the FFN to implement the Kronecker product in our proof; therefore, the universal approximation property of FFNs is also required.</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition E.2</span></span><span id="A5.Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Barron space <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">E et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">E et al., 2021</a>; <a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al., 2020</a>)</cite>)<span id="A5.Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Consider functions <math id="A5.Thmdefinition2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to\mathbb{R}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>ℝ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to\mathbb{R}</annotation></semantics></math> that admit the following representation:
<math id="A5.Thmdefinition2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\bm{x})=\int_{\Omega}a\sigma(\bm{b}^{\top}\bm{x}+c)\rho(\mathrm{d}a,\mathrm{d}\bm{b},\mathrm{d}c),\ \bm{x}\in X" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo>∫</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Ω</mi></msub><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>𝒃</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝒙</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ρ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>𝒃</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.667em">,</mo><mrow><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\bm{x})=\int_{\Omega}a\sigma(\bm{b}^{\top}\bm{x}+c)\rho(\mathrm{d}a,\mathrm{d}\bm{b},\mathrm{d}c),\ \bm{x}\in X</annotation></semantics></math>.
For any <math id="A5.Thmdefinition2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in[1,+\infty]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in[1,+\infty]</annotation></semantics></math>, we define the Barron norm as <math id="A5.Thmdefinition2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\|{f}\|_{\mathcal{B}_{p}}:=\inf_{\rho}\Big(\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[|a|^{p}(\|{\bm{b}}\|_{1}+|c|)^{p}\right]\Big)^{1/p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">:=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0em">inf</mo><mi>ρ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mi>ρ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>a</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>𝒃</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>c</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>p</mi></msup></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\|{f}\|_{\mathcal{B}_{p}}:=\inf_{\rho}\Big(\mathbb{E}_{\rho}\left[|a|^{p}(\|{\bm{b}}\|_{1}+|c|)^{p}\right]\Big)^{1/p}</annotation></semantics></math>.
Then the Barron space are defined as:
<math id="A5.Thmdefinition2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{B}_{p}:=\{f\in\mathcal{C}:\|{f}\|_{\mathcal{B}_{p}}&lt;+\infty\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒞</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{B}_{p}:=\{f\in\mathcal{C}:\|{f}\|_{\mathcal{B}_{p}}&lt;+\infty\}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma5" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmlemma5.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma E.5</span></span><span id="A5.Thmlemma5.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib43" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ma et al. (2020)</a></cite>)<span id="A5.Thmlemma5.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For any <math id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{B}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{B}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a two-layer ReLU neural network <math id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{FFN}(\bm{x})=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{K}a_{k}\sigma(\bm{b}_{k}^{\top}\bm{x}+c_{k})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>FFN</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐱</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>K</mi></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐛</mi><mi>k</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐱</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{FFN}(\bm{x})=\sum\limits_{k=1}^{K}a_{k}\sigma(\bm{b}_{k}^{\top}\bm{x}+c_{k})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A5.Thmlemma5.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> neurons such that</span></p>
<table id="A5.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex72"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex72.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|{f-\mathrm{FFN}}\|_{L^{\infty}[-2,2]}\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{\|{f}\|_{\mathcal{B}}\sqrt{\log K}}{\sqrt{K}}\right)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>FFN</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>L</mi><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℬ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msqrt></mrow><msqrt><mi>K</mi></msqrt></mfrac></mstyle><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|{f-\mathrm{FFN}}\|_{L^{\infty}[-2,2]}\leq\mathcal{O}\left(\frac{\|{f}\|_{\mathcal{B}}\sqrt{\log K}}{\sqrt{K}}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p16" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p16.1" class="ltx_p">We now present the approximation and tradeoff result:</p>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Tradeoff for Nonlinear Target)<span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">To approximate the target <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{\infty}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{\infty}\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐗</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋯</mo><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msubsup><msup><mi mathvariant="normal">H</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><msub><mi>𝐱</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{H}_{t}(\bm{X})=\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{\infty}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{\infty}\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math>, we employ <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>M</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M</annotation></semantics></math> groups of heads, where group <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math> contains <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> heads each of dimension <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{m}\leq d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{m}\leq d</annotation></semantics></math>. Given the model dimension <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\sum_{m=1}^{M}H_{m}\cdot d_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\sum_{m=1}^{M}H_{m}\cdot d_{m}</annotation></semantics></math> is fixed, with probability at least <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex73" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex73X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex73X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{D}(\bm{X})\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{D}(\bm{X})\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex73X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{M}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{M}\big\|\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big\|_{2}(1+\varepsilon_{\delta})^{n}\mathbb{I}_{\{\min_{m}d_{m}\leq d\}}\sqrt{1-\left(\tfrac{\min_{m}d_{m}}{d}\right)^{n}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mi>𝕀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{M}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{M}\big\|\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big\|_{2}(1+\varepsilon_{\delta})^{n}\mathbb{I}_{\{\min_{m}d_{m}\leq d\}}\sqrt{1-\left(\tfrac{\min_{m}d_{m}}{d}\right)^{n}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex73Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex73Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{M}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{M}\big\|\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big\|_{2}\Big[(B+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}})^{n}-B^{n}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>Attn</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{M}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{M}\big\|\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big\|_{2}\Big[(B+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}})^{n}-B^{n}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex73Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex73Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{H}}+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{FFN}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>FFN</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{H}}+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{FFN}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">where</span></p>
<table id="A5.Ex74" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex74X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex74X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex74X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sqrt{\tfrac{2\log(2ML/\delta)}{\min_{m}d_{m}}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msqrt><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>/</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sqrt{\tfrac{2\log(2ML/\delta)}{\min_{m}d_{m}}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex74Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex74Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>Attn</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex74Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\max_{m}\frac{1.3\,e^{0.02T}}{H_{m}}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>m</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>1.3</mn><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mn>0.02</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>T</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\max_{m}\frac{1.3\,e^{0.02T}}{H_{m}},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex74Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex74Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\varepsilon_{\mathrm{H}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>H</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\varepsilon_{\mathrm{H}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex74Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\Bigg\|\sum\limits_{\tau_{1}=0}^{\infty}\cdots\sum\limits_{\tau_{n}=0}^{\infty}\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.600em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Bigg\|\sum\limits_{\tau_{1}=0}^{\infty}\cdots\sum\limits_{\tau_{n}=0}^{\infty}\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex74Xc"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex74Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum\limits_{\tau_{1}=0}^{M}\cdots\sum\limits_{\tau_{n}=0}^{M}\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)\Bigg\|_{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="2.600em" rspace="0.0835em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0.0835em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum\limits_{\tau_{1}=0}^{M}\cdots\sum\limits_{\tau_{n}=0}^{M}\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)\Bigg\|_{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">and <math id="A5.Thmtheorem1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon_{\mathrm{FFN}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ε</mi><mi>FFN</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon_{\mathrm{FFN}}</annotation></semantics></math> is caused by using FFN to implement Kronecker product.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.Thmcorollary1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A5.Thmcorollary1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary E.1</span></span><span id="A5.Thmcorollary1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Parameter allocation via trade-offs)<span id="A5.Thmcorollary1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A5.Thmcorollary1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.Thmcorollary1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.Thmcorollary1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Under the same condition of Theorem <a href="#A5.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem E.1 (Tradeoff for Nonlinear Target). ‣ E.2 Continuous Time-homogeneous System ‣ Appendix E Approximation and tradeoff results for nonlinear target ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a>, the allocation of parameters can be achieved by solving the following optimization problem</span></p>
<table id="A5.E9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A5.E9X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E9X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\min_{M,\,H_{m},\,d_{m}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><munder><mi>min</mi><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow></munder><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\min_{M,\,H_{m},\,d_{m}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E9X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{M}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{M}\big\|\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="1.200em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{M}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{M}\big\|\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E9Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E9Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\times\left[\mathbb{I}_{\{\min_{m}d_{m}\leq d\}}\sqrt{1-\left(\tfrac{\min_{m}d_{m}}{d}\right)^{n}}+(B+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}})^{n}-B^{n}\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>𝕀</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>min</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mi>d</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>d</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></msub><msqrt><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>min</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup></mrow></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>Attn</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>B</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msup><mo>]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\times\left[\mathbb{I}_{\{\min_{m}d_{m}\leq d\}}\sqrt{1-\left(\tfrac{\min_{m}d_{m}}{d}\right)^{n}}+(B+\varepsilon_{\mathrm{Attn}})^{n}-B^{n}\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="A5.E9Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E9Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\text{s.t.}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtext class="ltx_mathvariant_italic">s.t.</mtext><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\text{s.t.}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.E9Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sum_{m=1}^{M}H_{m}\cdot d_{m}=D." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover></mstyle><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>D</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sum_{m=1}^{M}H_{m}\cdot d_{m}=D.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.5" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="A5.SS2.p17" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p17.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p17.1.1" class="ltx_text">In this proof, the construction of the embedding layer and the multi-head attention layer follows exactly the same procedure as in Theorem <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem1" title="Theorem 4.1. ‣ Linear sequence modeling. ‣ 4 Parameter trade-offs in Information Extraction ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. After these two steps, for each token, we obtain:</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p18" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A5.Ex75" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A5.Ex75.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\begin{pmatrix}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\\
0\\
\vdots\\
0\end{pmatrix}\longrightarrow\begin{pmatrix}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\\
\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-1}\\
\vdots\\
\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-M}\\
\bm{0}_{D-(M+1)\times d_{H}}\end{pmatrix}:=\bm{x}_{t}^{(1/2)}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>0</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">⟶</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mtable displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msub><mn>𝟎</mn><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>H</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub></mtd></mtr></mtable><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>:=</mo><msubsup><mi>𝒙</mi><mi>t</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\begin{pmatrix}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\\
0\\
\vdots\\
0\end{pmatrix}\longrightarrow\begin{pmatrix}\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t}\\
\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-1}\\
\vdots\\
\tilde{\bm{x}}_{t-M}\\
\bm{0}_{D-(M+1)\times d_{H}}\end{pmatrix}:=\bm{x}_{t}^{(1/2)}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p19" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A5.SS2.p19.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A5.SS2.p19.1.1" class="ltx_text">By Lemma <a href="#A2.Thmlemma2" title="Lemma B.2 (High-probability projection). ‣ Appendix B Lemmas used in Proofs ‣ Allocation of Parameters in Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>, with probability at least
<math id="A5.SS2.p19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-M\max_{m}2\exp\Big(-\frac{d_{m}\varepsilon^{2}}{2}\Big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-M\max_{m}2\exp\Big(-\frac{d_{m}\varepsilon^{2}}{2}\Big)</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A5.SS2.p20" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="A5.Ex76" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A5.Ex76X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex76X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{D}(\bm{X})=" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>D</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝑿</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mphantom></mphantom></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{E}_{D}(\bm{X})=</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex76X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\|\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{\infty}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{\infty}\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></msup><mi>H</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mi>𝒙</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\|\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{\infty}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{\infty}\mathrm{H}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\bm{x}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex76Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex76Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle-\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{M}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{M}\tilde{\mathrm{H}}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0.167em">⋯</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo></mstyle><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>M</mi></msup><mover accent="true"><mi>H</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>n</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>τ</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mo lspace="0.055em" rspace="0.055em">⋯</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⊗</mo><mover accent="true"><mi>𝒙</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>n</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em">∥</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle-\sum_{\tau_{1}=0}^{M}\cdots\sum_{\tau_{n}=0}^{M}\tilde{\mathrm{H}}^{(n)}(\tau_{1},\ldots,\tau_{n})\big(\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-\tau_{1}}\otimes\cdots\otimes\hat{\bm{x}}_{t-\tau_{n}}\big)\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A5.Ex76Xb"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A5.Ex76Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>≤</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq</annotation></semantics></math></td>
